Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-04-20
Subject: Use pai_symbol_end in the ait_symbol_end branch of the AT&T writer (fpc 0.99)
License: expat

In compiler/ag386att.pas the `ait_symbol_end' arm of the emit case
reads the symbol name like:

    AsmWrite(pai_symbol(hp)^.sym^.name);

but inside this arm `hp^.typ = ait_symbol_end', which means the
actual record is a tai_symbol_end -- a sibling of tai_symbol in the
pai hierarchy with a different layout.  The two records happen to
expose a `sym' field at the same byte offset, so on native FPC the
wrong cast reads the right bytes by coincidence.  Under the tp2cc
C++ bootstrap the emitter renders the cast as a checked downcast
onto an unrelated record type, and the cast is rejected at runtime
before the read can take place.

Fix: cast to pai_symbol_end, the actual record type.

--- a/compiler/ag386att.pas
+++ b/compiler/ag386att.pas
@@ -679,6 +679,12 @@
              end;

            ait_symbol_end :
+             { hp^.typ is ait_symbol_end here: the actual record is a
+               tai_symbol_end, a sibling of tai_symbol with a different
+               layout.  They happen to share a `sym' field at the same
+               offset so the old pai_symbol(hp) cast read the right bytes
+               by luck on native FPC.  Use pai_symbol_end, the correct
+               type. }
              begin
                if target_info.target=target_i386_linux then
                 begin
@@ -686,9 +692,9 @@
                   inc(symendcount);
                   AsmWriteLn(s+':');
                   AsmWrite(#9'.size'#9);
-                  AsmWrite(pai_symbol(hp)^.sym^.name);
+                  AsmWrite(pai_symbol_end(hp)^.sym^.name);
                   AsmWrite(', '+s+' - ');
-                  AsmWriteLn(pai_symbol(hp)^.sym^.name);
+                  AsmWriteLn(pai_symbol_end(hp)^.sym^.name);
                 end;
              end;

